    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-02-06",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Safe Passage on Interstates Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill establishes a new federal criminal offense for the obstruction of interstate highways.</p><p>Specifically, the bill makes it unlawful to knowingly engage in a listed activity with the intent to obstruct the free, convenient, and normal use of the interstate highway. The listed activities are (1) deliberately delaying traffic, (2) standing or approaching a motor vehicle, or (3) endangering the safe movement of a motor vehicle.</p><p>A violation is subject to criminal penalties.</p><p>The bill provides an exception for any lawful activity conducted or authorized by the federal government or by a state or local government.</p>",
        "update_date": "2025-03-24T20:39:34Z"
      }
    ]
  },
